    {
      "id": "p0094-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Toby noted that this is a reference to American medicine and toothpaste commercials that use the cliché “X out of Y professionals recommend” phrase. He also pointed out that part of the joke is about how there is always that one weird person who disagrees for some reason. Except in this case, it’s a rock.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.2905782,
          0.3235714,
          0.9114981,
          0.3964286
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.2905782,
          0.3235714,
          0.9114981,
          0.3964286
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Toby 说明，这句话是在模仿美国药品和牙膏广告常用的套话：“每 Y 位专业人士中，有 X 位推荐。”笑点还在于，总会有一个古怪的家伙，不知为什么就是持不同意见。只不过，这次那个家伙是一块石头。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.293637,
          0.325,
          0.9084393,
          0.4021429
        ],
        "font_size": 19,
        "line_height": 1.4210526315789473,
        "font_weight": 450,
