    {
      "id": "p0094-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The “X out of Y professionals recommend” phrase has been a part of Western pop culture for decades, but is largely unknown in Japan. As such, the reference would be lost in a straightforward translation. The localization team looked for a good Japanese equivalent, but nothing quite fit. So, they instead focused on the sign’s other two functions: providing a hint for proceeding in the game, and warning the player that one of the rocks might be strange. Thus, the final Japanese line became a literal, straightforward statement:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.2905782,
          0.57,
          0.9114981,
          0.6985714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.2905782,
          0.57,
          0.9114981,
          0.6985714
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "“每 Y 位专业人士中有 X 位推荐”几十年来一直是西方流行文化的一部分，在日本却鲜为人知。因此，直接翻译就会丢掉这个典故。团队尝试寻找贴切的日语表达，却始终没有合适的。于是，他们转而关注牌子的另外两项作用：提供推进游戏的提示，并提醒玩家，其中一块石头可能有点怪。最终，日版改成了一句平实的说明，大意是：",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.2946565,
          0.5678571,
          0.9094589,
